{
  "$comment": [
    "Ground truth is the CARD (canonicalName), not the string. A condition scores a",
    "hit when the resolver returns this card, regardless of what the ASR text was.",
    "",
    "spokenForms are what a player actually says at the table, including partial and",
    "nickname forms and some disfluency. RECORDING.md turns these into the read",
    "script; every spokenForm should get recorded at least once per speaker.",
    "",
    "Categories:",
    "  baseline          phonetically clean, common English. Should need no keyterm.",
    "  invented-noun     fabricated proper nouns with no English prior.",
    "  homophone         collides with a common English word or phrase.",
    "  card-collision    a wrong match here is a real gameplay error, not a typo.",
    "  possessive        apostrophe-s forms that normalization must handle.",
    "  nickname          the community name, which is what players say out loud.",
    "  partial-legendary players say the first word, never the full legendary name."
  ],
